ocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible with\nv4.6.1.stable.official [14d19694e]\nv4.7.2.stable.official [ed1daf0bf]\n\n\n### System information\n\nmacOS - Apple Silicon\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a RichTextLabel or Label processes the specific Devanagari script combination 'भै' (the base consonant 'भ' paired with the overhead vowel modifier ai-matra 'ै'), the engine logs a strict validation error:\n\nERROR: ./core/math/rect2i.h:111 - Rect2i size is negative, this is not supported. Use Rect2i.abs() to get a Rect2i with a positive size.\n\nThe text actually renders perfectly fine on screen with no visual artifacts.\n\nHighly Specific Trigger Details:\n• Font Dependency: This issue is highly reproduction-specific to the NotoSansDevanagari-VariableFont_wdth,wght.ttf font file.\n• Size Dependency: The error occurs only when the font size is set to exactly 32. Changing the font size to 40 stops the error.\n• Character Dependency: It is isolated purely to the 'भै' syllable cluster.\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new scene with a Control node.\n2. Add a RichTextLabel or a standard Label.\n3. Paste the character cluster भै (or the word भैंस) into the Text property.\n4. Set the font size to exactly 32.\n5. Create a global class with following effective font registration\n\nThemeDB.fallback_font.fallbacks.append(FONT_HINDI)\n \n6. Run the scene and observe the Debugger -> Errors\n7. Make the font manager script a tool script and the error comes in Editor -> Output Logs too.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[RTLBug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33437043/RTLBug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/u